# A server that refuses every connection: the wait doubles from 5 s and
# stops growing at 300 s: 5, 10, 20, 40, 80, 160, 300, 300. Each wait is
# shortened by up to a tenth, derived from the server id and the failure
# count, so the numbers are the same in every run. The console rounds the
# wait up to whole seconds.
! connect
> dial #1 irc.test:6667 plain
? notice Connecting to irc.test:6667
! closed error Connection refused
? notice Disconnected: Connection refused; reconnecting in 5 s
? failures 1
? waiting 4.965s
@ wake
> dial #2 irc.test:6667 plain
? notice Connecting to irc.test:6667
! closed error Connection refused
? notice Disconnected: Connection refused; reconnecting in 10 s
? failures 2
? waiting 9.947s
@ wake
